WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.779
Difficult Conversations.

2
00:00:02.059 --> 00:00:06.113
Day 72 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:08.887
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:13.092
The conversation you're avoiding is usually the one you most need to have.

5
00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:19.281
Stay calm, be specific, focus on the issue and not the person, and look for what both of you want.

6
00:00:20.631 --> 00:00:21.485
Part 1.

7
00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:23.087
The 5-step model.

8
00:00:24.337 --> 00:00:25.255
Step 1:

9
00:00:25.535 --> 00:00:27.881
Prepare: facts, your goal, their likely view.

10
00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.079
Step 2:

11
00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:30.447
Open safely:

12
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:32.220
I'd like to talk about X.

13
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.527
I want us both to come out of this better.

14
00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:35.724
Step 3:

15
00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:37.561
Share facts, then feelings:

16
00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:39.612
When X happened, I felt Y.

17
00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:40.852
Step 4:

18
00:00:41.132 --> 00:00:42.561
Listen and understand:

19
00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.399
Help me understand your side.

20
00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:45.639
Step 5:

21
00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:49.097
Agree on next steps: specific, written, with owners.

22
00:00:50.447 --> 00:00:51.322
Part 2.

23
00:00:51.602 --> 00:00:52.391
Scripts.

24
00:00:53.641 --> 00:00:54.601
Saying no.

25
00:00:54.881 --> 00:00:55.820
You could say:

26
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.428
I can't take this on this sprint without dropping the payments work.

27
00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:00.945
Which should come first?

28
00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.703
Other ways to say no:

29
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:06.309
Not right now, but I can look at it on Monday.

30
00:01:06.589 --> 00:01:08.338
I'm not the best person for this.

31
00:01:08.618 --> 00:01:10.346
Priya knows that system better.

32
00:01:10.626 --> 00:01:13.847
I can do part of it: the API, but not the UI.

33
00:01:15.197 --> 00:01:16.627
Disagreeing with a senior.

34
00:01:16.907 --> 00:01:17.845
You could say:

35
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:21.539
I respect your experience here, so I want to share a different view.

36
00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:26.576
I'm worried that skipping integration tests will push bugs into production during the sale.

37
00:01:26.856 --> 00:01:29.096
Could we keep tests for the checkout path only?

38
00:01:29.376 --> 00:01:30.592
It adds half a day.

39
00:01:31.942 --> 00:01:33.179
Conflict with a peer.

40
00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:34.398
You could say:

41
00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:37.025
Can we talk about the last few code reviews?

42
00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:42.083
I've noticed my PRs sit for 3 to 4 days, and some comments felt quite harsh.

43
00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.750
I might be misreading it.

44
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.118
How do you see it?

45
00:01:45.398 --> 00:01:47.254
I'd like us to work better together.

46
00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:49.948
Receiving criticism.

47
00:01:50.228 --> 00:01:50.975
Breathe.

48
00:01:51.255 --> 00:01:52.663
Don't reply instantly.

49
00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:53.775
Thank them:

50
00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:55.697
Thanks for telling me directly.

51
00:01:55.977 --> 00:01:56.916
Clarify:

52
00:01:57.196 --> 00:01:58.689
Can you give me an example?

53
00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:00.015
Own what's true:

54
00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:01.681
You're right, I missed that.

55
00:02:01.961 --> 00:02:02.644
Commit:

56
00:02:02.924 --> 00:02:04.033
Next time I'll...

57
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:06.130
Warning:

58
00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.242
Avoid.

59
00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:08.503
Yes, but...

60
00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:11.194
That's not fair, or bringing up their mistakes.

61
00:02:11.474 --> 00:02:16.935
Even if they're partly wrong, understand first, respond later (you can follow up the next day).

62
00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:19.949
Someone takes credit for your work.

63
00:02:20.229 --> 00:02:21.168
You could say:

64
00:02:21.448 --> 00:02:25.160
(Privately) In the demo, the caching work was presented as yours.

65
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.741
I built most of it.

66
00:02:27.021 --> 00:02:30.691
I'd appreciate it if we credit each other accurately going forward.

67
00:02:30.971 --> 00:02:32.208
Can we agree on that?

68
00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:37.462
(Publicly, at the next chance) As I mentioned when I built the cache layer...

69
00:02:38.812 --> 00:02:40.284
An angry stakeholder.

70
00:02:40.564 --> 00:02:41.503
You could say:

71
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:43.468
I understand you're frustrated.

72
00:02:43.748 --> 00:02:45.540
This outage hurt your customers.

73
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.191
Here's what we know, what we're doing, and when you'll hear from me next.

74
00:02:50.541 --> 00:02:54.679
Acknowledge the emotion, then give facts, then commit to the next update.

75
00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:56.389
Don't argue about blame.

76
00:02:57.739 --> 00:02:58.635
Part 3.

77
00:02:58.915 --> 00:03:00.707
Phrases that calm things down.

78
00:03:01.957 --> 00:03:03.322
Here is a quick table:

79
00:03:03.602 --> 00:03:04.711
Instead of, and Say.

80
00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:05.845
You're wrong.:

81
00:03:06.125 --> 00:03:07.405
I see it differently.

82
00:03:07.685 --> 00:03:08.709
You always...:

83
00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:10.802
In the last two sprints, I noticed...

84
00:03:11.082 --> 00:03:12.383
That's not my job.:

85
00:03:12.663 --> 00:03:15.842
I can't own that, but let me connect you with someone who can.

86
00:03:16.122 --> 00:03:17.103
Calm down.:

87
00:03:17.383 --> 00:03:19.026
I can see this matters a lot.

88
00:03:19.306 --> 00:03:20.501
Let's figure it out.

89
00:03:20.781 --> 00:03:21.890
Whatever, fine.:

90
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.559
I'm not fully convinced, but I'll commit to it.

91
00:03:24.839 --> 00:03:26.290
Let's review in 2 weeks.

92
00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.557
Part 4.

93
00:03:28.837 --> 00:03:30.224
Practice conversation:

94
00:03:30.504 --> 00:03:32.509
Disagreeing with a senior colleague.

95
00:03:33.759 --> 00:03:35.786
Here is how the conversation goes.

96
00:03:36.066 --> 00:03:38.477
Let's skip the integration tests this sprint.

97
00:03:38.757 --> 00:03:40.015
We don't have time.

98
00:03:40.295 --> 00:03:41.511
I see why.

99
00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:43.477
Can I share a concern?

100
00:03:43.757 --> 00:03:44.738
Go ahead.

101
00:03:45.018 --> 00:03:46.661
The sale is next week.

102
00:03:46.941 --> 00:03:52.125
Without integration tests on checkout, we could push a bug that costs us orders.

103
00:03:52.405 --> 00:03:54.197
But the tests take two days.

104
00:03:55.547 --> 00:03:57.147
The conversation continues.

105
00:03:57.427 --> 00:03:59.581
What if we only test the checkout path?

106
00:03:59.861 --> 00:04:01.419
That takes half a day.

107
00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:03.661
Okay, that's a fair compromise.

108
00:04:03.941 --> 00:04:05.584
Let's do checkout only.

109
00:04:05.864 --> 00:04:06.675
Thanks.

110
00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:08.555
I'll set it up today.

111
00:04:09.905 --> 00:04:11.441
That's the end of this lesson.

112
00:04:11.721 --> 00:04:16.393
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

113
00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:22.774
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

